  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 220 AM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nThe hot temperatures will spread back north on Tuesday as the\nfront dissipates and southerly flow returns across the area.\n\nThe operational medium-range models and many of the ensemble\nmembers are now trending toward the upper ridge shifting to the \nwest and northwest flow aloft developing over the central and \nsouthern Plains by late in the week, so we may be trending toward \nseeing some lower temperatures late in the week. NBM still keeps\ntemperature higher late next week than this pattern would suggest,\nbut that will start catching up if this signal shows more run-to-\nrun consistency. Despite the model trend showing this potential of\nshifting to northwest flow aloft, the precipitation chances\nassociated with this shift are still a little uncertain and\ndependent on how much of the ridge still reaches into the southern\nPlains.",
